11.79405],[46.5727,11.79377],[46.57283,11.79277],[46.57243,11.79217],[46.57211,11.79118],[46.57172,11.79059],[46.57105,11.78887],[46.57104,11.7884],[46.57118,11.78794],[46.57111,11.78756],[46.57091,11.78733],[46.57036,11.78713],[46.56993,11.78627],[46.56955,11.78589],[46.56903,11.78501],[46.56877,11.78416],[46.56765,11.78313]]', '[[46.554,11.8,2288,0],[46.56113,11.81592,2464,2],[46.5646,11.8228,2526,2.8],[46.56814,11.82536,2380,3.6],[46.577,11.83759,2366,5.6],[46.59003,11.82922,2479,7.6],[46.57332,11.79615,1771,12.5],[46.56765,11.78313,1659,14.1]]', '/gpx/selva-rifugio-puez.gpx', 'A committing high-alpine day on the lunar Puez plateau: from the Dantercepies gondola over Passo Cir and Passo Crespeina (2,528 m), past the emerald Lago di Crespeina to Rifugio Puez, returning down the long, dramatic Vallunga valley to Selva. No via ferrata — just distance, altitude and weather.'),
  (2, 'zelenci-nature-reserve', 'Zelenci Nature Reserve', 'Upper Sava Valley', 'Boardwalk loop', 'easy', 1, 'Out & back', 'Year-round', 1.4, 30, 0.5, 864, 'Zelenci Springs viewing platform', 'Ponce ridge / Mojstrovka, Karavanke to the north', '5 km west of Kranjska Gora on road 202 toward Rateče; free parking at Gostilna Zelenci, then a flat boardwalk. Also a lovely ~1 h walk or bike ride from town along the valley path.', 46.4943, 13.7344, 46.4924, 13.7378, '[[46.49427,13.73452],[46.494,13.73434],[46.49382,13.73441],[46.49333,13.73507],[46.49297,13.736],[46.49274,13.737],[46.49254,13.73729],[46.49253,13.73763],[46.49254,13.73729],[46.49274,13.737],[46.49292,13.73622],[46.49283,13.73482],[46.492,13.7346],[46.49141,13.7349],[46.49083,13.73458],[46.49047,13.73494],[46.49013,13.73595],[46.49098,13.74036]]', '[[46.49427,13.73452,841,0],[46.49309,13.73577,838,0.2],[46.49253,13.73763,835,0.4],[46.49098,13.74036,841,1.3]]', '/gpx/zelenci-nature-reserve.gpx', 'A short, magical boardwalk leads through reed-fringed wetland to the turquoise springs where the Sava Dolinka, Slovenia''s longest river, bubbles up from the lake bed. The shallow emerald pool shimmers below the Ponce peaks, with a wooden observation tower and rich birdlife making it a perfect, stroller-friendly family stop.'),
  (2, 'lake-jasna-loop', 'Lake Jasna Walk', 'Kranjska Gora / Pišnica valley', 'Circular trail', 'easy', 0, 'Loop', 'Year-round', 2.9, 36, 0.8, 837, 'Lake Jasna', 'Prisojnik / Razor at the head of the Vršič valley', 'Starts at the Kranjska Gora tourist information centre; a flat forest path follows the Pišnica river ~1.5 km south to the lake. Parking at Lake Jasna itself for those who drive.', 46.4851, 13.7844, 46.4741, 13.784, '[[46.48531,13.78461],[46.48501,13.78567],[46.48455,13.78574],[46.48424,13.78491],[46.48294,13.78612],[46.4823,13.7844],[46.48197,13.78391],[46.4823,13.7844],[46.48294,13.78612],[46.48233,13.78633],[46.48244,13.78581],[46.48223,13.78581],[46.48215,13.78546],[46.48114,13.78483],[46.48089,13.78495],[46.48066,13.78539],[46.47988,13.78523],[46.47874,13.78462],[46.47792,13.78466],[46.47703,13.78546],[46.47676,13.78606],[46.47634,13.78644],[46.47579,13.78662],[46.47565,13.78656],[46.47581,13.78631],[46.47616,13.78427],[46.47619,13.78302],[46.47608,13.7827],[46.47547,13.7821],[46.47532,13.78281],[46.47521,13.78267],[46.47422,13.78293],[46.47442,13.78388]]', '[[46.48531,13.78461,807,0],[46.48197,13.78391,809,0.6],[46.47845,13.78459,892,1.5],[46.47618,13.78383,849,2.1],[46.47442,13.78388,833,2.5]]', '/gpx/lake-jasna-loop.gpx', 'An effortless riverside stroll from the town centre to a pair of dammed turquoise lakes that mirror the towering walls of Prisojnik and Razor. The famous golden Zlatorog (Goldenhorn) ibex statue stands lakeside, and cafés by the water make it an ideal gentle evening or family loop.'),
  (2, 'pericnik-waterfall', 'Peričnik Waterfall (Vrata Valley)', 'Triglav National Park · Vrata Valley', 'Circular trail behind the falls', 'easy', 0, 'Loop', 'May – Oct', 1, 120, 0.75, 881, 'Upper Peričnik viewpoint', 'Vrata valley walls beneath Triglav''s north face', 'Drive ~13 km from Kranjska Gora to Mojstrana, then 4.5 km up the Vrata valley road to the Koča pri Peričniku lodge; small paid parking. Short steep steps lead up to and behind the falls.', 46.4385, 13.8963, 46.4392, 13.8935, '[[46.43852,13.89618],[46.43874,13.89592],[46.4393,13.89569],[46.43906,13.89483],[46.4392,13.8951],[46.43936,13.8951],[46.43945,13.89402],[46.43911,13.89352],[46.43879,13.89381],[46.43879,13.8934],[46.43897,13.89329],[46.43892,13.89303],[46.4392,13.89345],[46.43892,13.89303],[46.43897,13.89329],[46.43879,13.8934],[46.43879,13.89381],[46.43911,13.89352],[46.43945,13.89402]]', '[[46.43852,13.89618,754,0],[46.43906,13.89483,794,0.2],[46.4392,13.89345,843,0.5],[46.43945,13.89402,819,0.3]]', '/gpx/pericnik-waterfall.gpx', 'A short but spectacular loop to one of Slovenia''s most famous waterfalls, where the Peričnik plunges 52 m in a single curtain you can actually walk behind on a rocky ledge. Set deep in the Vrata valley under the gateway to Triglav — dramatic, misty and unforgettable. Steps can be icy or closed in winter.'),
  (2, 'tamar-valley-planica', 'Tamar Valley to Dom v Tamarju', 'Triglav National Park · Tamar Valley', 'No. 206', 'easy', 1, 'Out & back', 'May – Oct', 7.2, 245, 2.5, 1108, 'Dom v Tamarju', 'Jalovec and the Ponce group; Mojstrovka above the valley head', 'Drive or cycle 4 km from Kranjska Gora via Rateče to the Planica Nordic Centre; paid parking. A wide gravel path climbs gently up the valley to the hut. Seasonal bus in summer.', 46.4771, 13.7249, 46.4461, 13.7134, '[[46.47708,13.72491],[46.47686,13.72401],[46.47659,13.72411],[46.47609,13.72386],[46.4755,13.72406],[46.47493,13.72289],[46.47475,13.72277],[46.47431,13.72284],[46.47413,13.72306],[46.47324,13.72345],[46.47225,13.72329],[46.47118,13.72335],[46.46965,13.72372],[46.46897,13.72352],[46.46835,13.72355],[46.46676,13.72284],[46.46634,13.72248],[46.46703,13.72227],[46.46727,13.71991],[46.46753,13.71887],[46.46802,13.7178],[46.46426,13.71804],[46.464,13.71823],[46.46176,13.71821],[46.4613,13.71783],[46.46016,13.71747],[46.45932,13.71671],[46.4586,13.71667],[46.4577,13.71621],[46.45576,13.71568],[46.45539,13.71543],[46.45466,13.71562],[46.45396,13.71604],[46.4536,13.71601],[46.45317,13.7155],[46.45289,13.71543],[46.45167,13.71582],[46.45129,13.71524],[46.4502,13.71456],[46.44917,13.71446],[46.44817,13.71409],[46.44791,13.71413],[46.4477,13.71458],[46.44727,13.71404],[46.44617,13.71342]]', '[[46.47708,13.72491,941,0],[46.47032,13.72353,994,0.9],[46.46202,13.71823,1056,2.5],[46.454,13.71603,1084,3.4],[46.44617,13.71342,1107,4.4]]', '/gpx/tamar-valley-planica.gpx', 'A broad, easy gravel track past the Planica ski-flying hills into a dramatic glacial cirque ringed by the Ponce peaks, with the spear-like summit of Jalovec rising at its head. The welcoming Dom v Tamarju hut serves traditional fare, and a short steep spur beyond reaches the Nadiža spring.'),
  (2, 'krnica-valley-hut', 'Krnica Valley to Koča v Krnici', 'Triglav National Park · Krnica Valley', 'Valley trail via Lake Jasna', 'easy', 0, 'Out & back', 'May – Oct', 9, 330, 3, 1113, 'Koča v Krnici', 'Razor, Prisojnik, Špik and Škrlatica walls ringing the cirque', 'From Kranjska Gora walk or drive ~1.5 km to Lake Jasna; the Krnica path branches off the Vršič road just before the Pišnica bridge, then a forest trail leads up the valley to the hut.', 46.4741, 13.784, 46.4324, 13.7876, '[[46.47442,13.78388],[46.47422,13.78293],[46.47514,13.78268],[46.47517,13.78235],[46.4754,13.78192],[46.47532,13.78146],[46.47418,13.7814],[46.47367,13.78096],[46.4732,13.78167],[46.46965,13.78201],[46.46921,13.78198],[46.46861,13.78125],[46.46799,13.78127],[46.46735,13.78173],[46.46693,13.78172],[46.46665,13.78207],[46.46711,13.78291],[46.46608,13.78347],[46.46504,13.7844],[46.46473,13.78442],[46.46414,13.78408],[46.46274,13.7847],[46.46179,13.78443],[46.46148,13.78459],[46.4607,13.78461],[46.46014,13.78432],[46.45961,13.78387],[46.45919,13.78288],[46.45888,13.78256],[46.45811,13.78305],[46.4575,13.78241],[46.45679,13.78318],[46.4563,13.78338],[46.456,13.78374],[46.45495,13.78375],[46.45444,13.78353],[46.45399,13.78288],[46.45254,13.78303],[46.4521,13.78278],[46.45081,13.78153],[46.45065,13.78106],[46.44832,13.7804],[46.44774,13.7805],[46.44724,13.78112],[46.4444,13.78131],[46.44399,13.78157],[46.44355,13.78146],[46.44322,13.78155],[46.4427,13.78313],[46.44271,13.78367],[46.44295,13.78405],[46.44282,13.78455],[46.44262,13.78446],[46.44261,13.78471],[46.44276,13.78488],[46.44245,13.78544],[46.44264,13.78613],[46.44282,13.78604],[46.44289,13.78625],[46.44272,13.78619],[46.44306,13.78707],[46.44304,13.78737],[46.44328,13.78774],[46.44304,13.78737],[46.44306,13.78707],[46.44272,13.78619],[46.44289,13.78625],[46.44282,13.78604],[46.44264,13.78613],[46.44245,13.78544],[46.44276,13.78488],[46.44261,13.78471],[46.44262,13.78446],[46.44282,13.78455],[46.44295,13.78405],[46.44271,13.78367],[46.4427,13.78313],[46.44322,13.78155],[46.44284,13.78148],[46.44251,13.78166],[46.44211,13.78079],[46.44143,13.78081],[46.44114,13.78111],[46.4408,13.78201],[46.44056,13.78224],[46.44026,13.78351],[46.4399,13.78416],[46.43819,13.78654],[46.43753,13.78683],[46.4356,13.7881],[46.43491,13.78828],[46.43454,13.78789],[46.43425,13.78802],[46.43337,13.78749],[46.43273,13.78739],[46.43244,13.78764]]', '[[46.47442,13.78388,833,0],[46.46552,13.78397,860,1.6],[46.456,13.78374,901,2.8],[46.44328,13.78774,1134,5],[46.43244,13.78764,1111,7.2]]', '/gpx/krnica-valley-hut.gpx', 'From Lake Jasna a serene forest trail climbs gently into the wild Krnica glacial valley, hemmed in by the sheer north faces of Razor, Prisojnik and Škrlatica. One of the easiest yet most scenic alpine-cirque walks around Kranjska Gora, with a cosy hut at the valley''s end.'),
  (2, 'vrsic-huts-ajdovska-deklica', 'Vršič Pass Hut Walk & Ajdovska Deklica View', 'Triglav National Park', 'Tičarjev dom – Poštarski dom', 'easy', 0, 'Out & back', 'May – Oct', 2, 110, 0.75, 1725, 'Poštarski dom', 'Prisojnik north face & window, Ajdovska deklica rock face', 'Top of the Vršič Pass (1611 m), 13 km and 24 hairpins from Kranjska Gora; park at the pass by Tičarjev dom, then walk the gravel road ~10 min up to Poštarski dom.', 46.4327, 13.7446, 46.4324, 13.7475, '[[46.43264,13.74453],[46.4326,13.74492],[46.43271,13.74523],[46.43244,13.74576],[46.43197,13.74625],[46.43155,13.74697],[46.43097,13.74729],[46.43036,13.74812],[46.43076,13.74813],[46.431,13.74784],[46.4312,13.74811],[46.4324,13.7471],[46.43247,13.74718],[46.43232,13.74743]]', '[[46.43264,13.74453,1614,0],[46.43244,13.74576,1632,0.1],[46.43232,13.74743,1692,0.7]]', '/gpx/vrsic-huts-ajdovska-deklica.gpx', 'A short, family-friendly stroll between two classic mountain huts at the crown of the Vršič Pass. From Poštarski dom you look straight at the towering Prisojnik north wall, its natural rock window, and the eerie ''Pagan Girl'' (Ajdovska deklica) face the erosion carved into the cliff. Big-mountain atmosphere with almost no climbing.'),
  (2, 'slemenova-spica-vrsic', 'Slemenova Špica (Sleme)', 'Triglav National Park', 'Vršič – Sleme', 'easy', 1, 'Out & back', 'Jun – Oct', 5.7, 450, 3, 1911, 'Slemenova Špica', 'Jalovec, Prisojnik, Mojstrovka, Trenta valley', 'Drive the Vršič Pass road from Kranjska Gora (~13 km, 24 hairpins) to the top of the pass at 1611 m; park at the pass. Trail starts near Tičarjev dom.', 46.4348, 13.7437, 46.446, 13.7265, '[[46.43479,13.74372],[46.43505,13.74371],[46.43512,13.74344],[46.43502,13.74306],[46.43461,13.74261],[46.43435,13.74183],[46.43439,13.74093],[46.43423,13.73986],[46.43402,13.73968],[46.43393,13.73909],[46.4335,13.73871],[46.43338,13.73823],[46.43306,13.73816],[46.43256,13.73739],[46.43226,13.73722],[46.43396,13.73676],[46.43449,13.73682],[46.43521,13.73737],[46.43615,13.73708],[46.43645,13.73685],[46.43668,13.73631],[46.43724,13.73618],[46.43791,13.73578],[46.43802,13.73527],[46.43792,13.73513],[46.43788,13.73452],[46.43801,13.73402],[46.43788,13.73452],[46.43792,13.73513],[46.43802,13.73527],[46.43791,13.73578],[46.43724,13.73618],[46.43668,13.73631],[46.43645,13.73685],[46.43615,13.73708],[46.43521,13.73737],[46.43449,13.73682],[46.43396,13.73676],[46.43226,13.73722],[46.43256,13.73739],[46.43306,13.73816],[46.43338,13.73823],[46.43353,13.73875],[46.43393,13.73909],[46.43402,13.73968],[46.43431,13.74013],[46.43435,13.74183],[46.43461,13.74261],[46.43502,13.74306],[46.43512,13.74344],[46.43505,13.74371],[46.4353,13.74405],[46.43584,13.7442],[46.437,13.7441],[46.43799,13.74376],[46.43863,13.7437],[46.43919,13.74335],[46.44001,13.74321],[46.44003,13.74306],[46.4402,13.74319],[46.44036,13.74278],[46.44063,13.74262],[46.44076,13.74232],[46.44121,13.7423],[46.44087,13.74099],[46.44066,13.73941],[46.43964,13.73689],[46.43952,13.73554],[46.43972,13.73441],[46.44004,13.73405],[46.44036,13.73304],[46.44082,13.73232],[46.44165,13.72819],[46.44227,13.72716],[46.4426,13.72694],[46.44289,13.72687],[46.44339,13.7272],[46.44384,13.72686],[46.44479,13.7266],[46.44494,13.72636],[46.44508,13.72644],[46.44531,13.72604],[46.446,13.72648]]', '[[46.43479,13.74372,1614,0],[46.43406,13.73973,1726,0.4],[46.43801,13.73402,2096,1.6],[46.44137,13.72984,1806,5],[46.446,13.72649,1897,5.7]]', '/gpx/slemenova-spica-vrsic.gpx', 'Slovenia''s most photographed ridge walk: a broad larch-and-pine ribbon of grassland from the Vršič Pass to a balcony summit. The reward is a jaw-dropping panorama of pyramid-shaped Jalovec, the sheer Prisojnik north face and the green depths of the Trenta valley. Short, mostly gentle, endlessly scenic.'),
  (2, 'tromeja-pec-ratece', 'Tromeja / Peč — Three-Country Border', 'Karavanke', 'Rateče – Peč', 'medium', 0, 'Out & back', 'Apr – Nov', 6.3, 640, 3, 1510, 'Peč (Tromeja)', 'Julian Alps panorama, Gailtal Alps, western Karavanke', 'Drive or take the bus to Rateče village (~6 km west of Kranjska Gora); park near the village. A marked trail climbs through forest to the summit; a gentler forest road makes a loop variant.', 46.4977, 13.7158, 46.523, 13.7141, '[[46.49794,13.71573],[46.49799,13.71643],[46.49822,13.71641],[46.49848,13.71611],[46.49974,13.71581],[46.50044,13.71597],[46.50056,13.71582],[46.50059,13.71521],[46.50037,13.71466],[46.50064,13.71476],[46.50168,13.71444],[46.50189,13.71501],[46.50168,13.71444],[46.50064,13.71476],[46.50037,13.71466],[46.50059,13.71521],[46.50056,13.71582],[46.50083,13.71559],[46.50101,13.71564],[46.50231,13.71701],[46.50258,13.71671],[46.50273,13.71569],[46.50284,13.71543],[46.50295,13.71545],[46.50325,13.71585],[46.50344,13.7167],[46.50571,13.71911],[46.50648,13.71766],[46.50672,13.71766],[46.50731,13.71847],[46.50759,13.71852],[46.5082,13.71719],[46.50881,13.71632],[46.50914,13.71607],[46.50983,13.71617],[46.51053,13.71669],[46.51107,13.71684],[46.5115,13.71725],[46.51208,13.71703],[46.51219,13.71757],[46.51239,13.71773],[46.51347,13.71722],[46.51385,13.71741],[46.51442,13.71731],[46.51528,13.71675],[46.51631,13.71642],[46.51626,13.71605],[46.51681,13.71585],[46.51708,13.71557],[46.51767,13.71418],[46.51789,13.71247],[46.5187,13.71005],[46.51887,13.70828],[46.51907,13.70767],[46.51902,13.70652],[46.51891,13.70606],[46.5195,13.70521],[46.51944,13.70592],[46.51963,13.70556],[46.52001,13.7055],[46.52082,13.70668],[46.52093,13.70699],[46.52081,13.70727],[46.5211,13.70783],[46.52101,13.70852],[46.5213,13.70963],[46.52126,13.71034],[46.52209,13.7116],[46.52279,13.71333],[46.52305,13.71364],[46.523,13.71409]]', '[[46.49794,13.71573,867,0],[46.50189,13.71501,913,0.7],[46.50905,13.71614,1096,2.3],[46.51626,13.71605,1190,3.2],[46.523,13.71409,1506,5.2]]', '/gpx/tromeja-pec-ratece.gpx', 'The westernmost summit of the Karavanke and a geography-lover''s prize: stand on the exact tripoint where Slovenia, Austria and Italy meet, marked by a three-sided peace monument. A steady forest climb from Rateče opens to a 360° sweep over the Julian Alps and the Tarvisio basin. Snow-free far longer than the high Julian peaks.'),
  (2, 'vitranc-ciprnik', 'Vitranc & Ciprnik', 'Triglav National Park', 'Via Mojčin dom', 'medium', 0, 'Out & back', 'May – Oct', 12, 940, 4.5, 1745, 'Ciprnik', 'Špik, Martuljek group, Razor, Prisojnik, Planica valley', 'On foot from Kranjska Gora centre via the Vitranc ski area; the Vitranc 1 chairlift (when running) shortcuts the lower climb. ~2 h to Vitranc, +1 h along the wooded crest to Ciprnik.', 46.4855, 13.7844, 46.4688, 13.74, '[[46.48546,13.78466],[46.48531,13.78461],[46.48501,13.78567],[46.48455,13.78574],[46.48419,13.78466],[46.48437,13.78353],[46.48473,13.78266],[46.48489,13.78038],[46.48542,13.77895],[46.48605,13.77771],[46.48603,13.77744],[46.4863,13.77671],[46.48655,13.77635],[46.4866,13.77546],[46.48683,13.7753],[46.48649,13.77479],[46.48608,13.77334],[46.48542,13.76994],[46.48506,13.76933],[46.4847,13.76813],[46.4847,13.76708],[46.4845,13.76599],[46.48504,13.76408],[46.48489,13.76264],[46.48476,13.76256],[46.48441,13.76154],[46.48404,13.76115],[46.48395,13.7613],[46.48367,13.76122],[46.48367,13.7617],[46.48352,13.76196],[46.48335,13.76147],[46.48309,13.76164],[46.48254,13.76165],[46.48184,13.76137],[46.48151,13.76113],[46.48104,13.76047],[46.48018,13.76004],[46.48006,13.75973],[46.48011,13.75875],[46.47995,13.75835],[46.47981,13.75844],[46.47969,13.75897],[46.47944,13.75859],[46.47943,13.75892],[46.47934,13.75894],[46.47888,13.75827],[46.47886,13.75902],[46.47853,13.75844],[46.47845,13.75844],[46.47839,13.75901],[46.47806,13.75857],[46.47815,13.75907],[46.4779,13.75918],[46.47774,13.7595],[46.47756,13.75917],[46.47714,13.75895],[46.47628,13.75873],[46.4763,13.75891],[46.47617,13.75879],[46.47617,13.75897],[46.47596,13.75888],[46.47595,13.75933],[46.47535,13.7581],[46.47519,13.75696],[46.47526,13.75641],[46.47502,13.75525],[46.47426,13.75382],[46.47387,13.75237],[46.47376,13.75098],[46.47326,13.74969],[46.4732,13.74816],[46.47336,13.74696],[46.4732,13.74563],[46.47279,13.74476],[46.47183,13.74392],[46.47143,13.74323],[46.47148,13.74344],[46.47134,13.74343],[46.47129,13.74385],[46.47118,13.74386],[46.47105,13.74357],[46.47106,13.74374],[46.47105,13.74357],[46.47118,13.74386],[46.47129,13.74385],[46.47134,13.74343],[46.47148,13.74344],[46.47088,13.74147],[46.46986,13.74102],[46.46984,13.74089],[46.46998,13.74085],[46.46971,13.74059],[46.46964,13.74023],[46.4689,13.74031],[46.46877,13.74002]]', '[[46.48546,13.78466,807,0],[46.485,13.76893,938,1.6],[46.47328,13.74974,1630,4.7],[46.47106,13.74374,1564,5.4],[46.46877,13.74002,1734,6]]', '/gpx/vitranc-ciprnik.gpx', 'A forested ridge climb from the resort up through Vitranc''s ski slopes to a quiet larch-clad summit looking straight down onto the Planica ski-jumps. The crest walk from Vitranc to Ciprnik delivers superb views of Špik and the jagged Martuljek wall. Riding the chairlift trims it to a half-day outing.'),
  (2, 'mala-mojstrovka-vratca', 'Mala Mojstrovka via Vratca', 'Triglav National Park', 'South route (cabled)', 'hard', 0, 'Out & back', 'Jul – Sep', 3.5, 720, 4, 2332, 'Mala Mojstrovka', 'Velika Mojstrovka, Travnik, Jalovec, Trenta valley', 'Top of the Vršič Pass (1611 m), reached by the hairpin road from Kranjska Gora; park at the pass. The trail branches off the Slemenova Špica path toward the Vratca saddle and up the south scree face.', 46.4348, 13.7437, 46.4374, 13.7311, '[[46.43479,13.74372],[46.43505,13.74371],[46.43512,13.74344],[46.43502,13.74306],[46.43461,13.74261],[46.43435,13.74183],[46.43439,13.74093],[46.43423,13.73986],[46.43402,13.73968],[46.43393,13.73909],[46.4335,13.73871],[46.43338,13.73823],[46.43306,13.73816],[46.43256,13.73739],[46.43226,13.73722],[46.43334,13.73683],[46.43421,13.73676],[46.43458,13.73687],[46.43521,13.73737],[46.43615,13.73708],[46.43645,13.73685],[46.43664,13.73636],[46.43645,13.73685],[46.43615,13.73708],[46.43521,13.73737],[46.43458,13.73687],[46.43421,13.73676],[46.43334,13.73683],[46.43226,13.73722],[46.4313,13.7368],[46.43124,13.73651],[46.43091,13.73624],[46.43037,13.73599],[46.43019,13.73609],[46.43032,13.73575],[46.43047,13.73569],[46.43054,13.73583],[46.43083,13.73533],[46.43127,13.73522],[46.43159,13.73461],[46.43247,13.73392],[46.43336,13.73199],[46.43451,13.73076],[46.43466,13.73123],[46.43499,13.7309],[46.43554,13.73078],[46.43588,13.73131],[46.43653,13.73093],[46.43668,13.73114],[46.4369,13.73117],[46.4371,13.7309],[46.43739,13.7311]]', '[[46.43479,13.74372,1614,0],[46.43431,13.74013,1719,0.4],[46.43664,13.73636,1965,1.2],[46.4369,13.73117,2308,3.1],[46.43739,13.7311,2322,3.2]]', '/gpx/mala-mojstrovka-vratca.gpx', 'A genuine alpine summit straight off the Vršič Pass: switchbacks up shifting scree to the Vratca saddle, then a short protected cable-and-steps section onto the 2332 m crown. The exposure and loose terrain demand sure feet and a head for heights, but the summit panorama over the Julian giants is immense. (The far harder Hanzova via ferrata climbs the north face.)'),
