],[46.43299,13.79297],[46.43296,13.79255],[46.43273,13.79218],[46.43274,13.79192],[46.43292,13.79159],[46.4328,13.79119],[46.43309,13.79061],[46.43355,13.79011],[46.43359,13.78971],[46.43292,13.78845],[46.43257,13.78812],[46.43254,13.78781],[46.43238,13.78781],[46.43243,13.78765]]', '[[46.43243,13.78765,1111,0],[46.43949,13.79796,1559,2.4],[46.4427,13.80626,2069,4.1],[46.44648,13.81223,2414,5],[46.44881,13.81435,2461,10.9],[46.44262,13.79946,1771,3.4],[46.43243,13.78765,1111,0]]', '/gpx/spik-krnica.gpx', 'A steep, sustained classic rising ~1600 m from the wild Krnica cirque to one of the most striking summits above Kranjska Gora. The Gruntovica line has short cabled sections and a crumbly ravine where a helmet is necessary; the often-wet Kačji graben is best kept for descent, making a natural loop. Long and strenuous — a single big day.'),
  (2, 'prisojnik-okno', 'Prisojnik via the Window (Okno) Route', 'Triglav National Park', 'Kopiščarjeva pot · VF B/C–C/D', 'hard', 0, 'Loop', 'Jul – Sep', 8.5, 1050, 7.5, 2547, 'Prisojnik (Prisank)', 'Prisojnik group, Razor, Julian Alps', 'From Kranjska Gora drive ~25 min up the Vršič road to the top of the pass (1611 m); large parking at the saddle by Tičarjev dom.', 46.4348, 13.7437, 46.4247, 13.7697, '[[46.4348,13.7437],[46.431,13.756],[46.43,13.765],[46.427,13.769],[46.4247,13.7697],[46.43,13.756],[46.4348,13.7437]]', '[]', NULL, 'The classic Julian Alps adventure: the Kopiščarjeva pot climbs the north face past the Ajdovska deklica and threads the spectacular ~100 m natural rock window (Okno) before reaching the summit ridge. Three short via-ferrata sections linked by long exposed scrambling — helmet and via-ferrata set mandatory. Descend the easier south-side Slovenska pot back to Vršič.'),
  (2, 'triglav-krma', 'Triglav via Krma Valley', 'Triglav National Park', 'Krma – Kredarica – summit', 'hard', 1, 'Out & back', 'Jul – Sep', 25, 2050, 12, 2864, 'Triglav', 'Triglav massif', 'From Kranjska Gora drive ~35 min east to Mojstrana, then up the Krma valley to the last parking at the barrier near Kovinarska koča (~900 m); the final ~6 km of road is gravel.', 46.4006, 13.9237, 46.3783, 13.8366, '[[46.4006,13.9237],[46.395,13.895],[46.385,13.87],[46.3789,13.8488],[46.3783,13.8366]]', '[]', NULL, 'Slovenia''s longest but technically gentlest way up its highest summit: a glacial-valley grind to the Kredarica plateau, then an airy cabled scramble up the summit pyramid. The final ridge has steel cables and pegs over big exposure — helmet (ideally a via-ferrata set) strongly recommended. Almost always done over two days with a night at Triglavski dom na Kredarici (2515 m) or the quieter Dom Planika.');
